msgid "Archived: Advanced MultiCopter Design"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:7
#: af82e71c84104bdd860c2eae86e1a3a5
msgid "This section is topics related to advanced multicopter construction and design."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:12
#: 272b82ce33404316ab1e614b013d4316
msgid "For information on understanding how a multicopter works please go :ref:`Here <what-is-a-multicopter-and-how-does-it-work>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:14
#: 8cd0e9ee182040db8da07f2c036dc34e
msgid "For information on how to build your own simple Quadcopter using kits or frames go :ref:`Here <build-your-own-multicopter>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:16
#: e3a7e7e346734d0fb8952fab3517fb1b
msgid "For information on building or setting up a copter for first Person View (FPV) go :ref:`Here <common-fpv-first-person-view>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:20
#: 780ab51cc2994ef2b1fd7768531420ed
msgid "There are several popular frame layouts for MultiCopters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:22
#: 34bbc406b50b418ebf1c1296a22a9be0
msgid "The Tricopter uses 3 motor / propeller propulsion units with a servo to rotate one of them to compensate for adverse yaw."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:25
#: 3311755a3777437d845f7f49d6403f8a
msgid "Tricopters were popular early on when the brushless motor / propeller units were new and scarce."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:27
#: d333f19451a14fcea994990ccb0dd602
msgid "They suffer from less than stellar performance and do not scale well to larger sizes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:29
#: 4b2b61bb4bae48f4bdf3177a77694832
msgid "But they still have some popularity for small, light hobby use applications."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:31
#: cd87bde5dac940fd976cc47aa1273a0e
msgid "Because this is primarily an outdated design we will not expand further on it in this article."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:37
#: 3f45f90e689d43d89b4aed0a5e9190a6
msgid "The very popular Quadcopter has 4 motor/propeller units and is available in any size."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:40
#: b310cab7a12a465c9c0a24cdbbc16a8a
msgid "A Quadcopter is an elegantly simple design and is hands down the most popular layout for a whole lot of reasons."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:42
#: 9dd75d9ea6d345e1bd05e4f62a7297f6
msgid "Quadcopters are symmetrical and embody the simplest principle of operation for controlling roll, pitch, yaw and motion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:44
#: ef1377891d064a55bae78f41d9d86ef1
msgid "Simply varying the speed of each of the motors provides full 3D motion and rotation and hover capability."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:46
#: 6f1d007eadd540a5a0b476fb089b2d69
msgid "They are relatively inexpensive to produce and they scale well to production manufacturing techniques."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:48
#: f62a008fc1d042e99a223b526c7e904c
msgid "In various sizes and layouts they are capable of actually performing useful tasks beyond simply flying around."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:50
#: 0b1be2b7342e413cabc544502922b920
msgid "Their primary drawback is that a single motor failure generally results in an abrupt descent to the ground (crash)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:52
#: 47c66e0e748c43a6ba181c2149def64a
msgid "A very wide variety of materials and techniques can be employed to produce a useful Quadcopter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:54
#: a201f0ec12f14e3abeb8ba9688e2d388
msgid "There are several popular configurations for QuadCopters:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:56
#: fd83bcfda3ce41b1ba28d855aecbbd25
msgid "X with and X frame arm layout and the front and back of the copter between 2 propellers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:58
#: 02fde19ba45145108d2221250f48d099
msgid "and with the same kind of X frame layout as above but with the front and back of the copter in line with one of the propellers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:61
#: e755a2f4d555482094e6a8b313356e49
msgid "\"Dead Cat\" a variation on X which in which the frame arms are further apart in the front and the back than they are side to side."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:65
#: 4d3c81ee3aad4515b024518f5a017f09
msgid "Name actually comes from Bart Jansen a Dutch artist who stuffed his expired cat and made a Quadcopter out of it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:68
#: ad771c55195241f09a2f9249fa42156c
msgid "H which has frame side arms running between the motors on each side and connected with one or more frame arms in the middle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:70
#: 7466d3df9f314686abf64d184b28a15a
msgid "Square which has frame arms connecting between motors (and usually intermediate frame arms supporting a central frame.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:72
#: 52c5d6621a6f45659356617bbd50690e
msgid "And variations including ones with the motors laid out on a circle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:74
#: 57622594dcef427da2148ff9587d3ac3
msgid "Most of them primarily operate the same as the X frame (provides better camera exposure between motors among other things)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:77
#: 005f5c2bf8f54069823f6279572f2983
msgid "I recommend the standard X frame design because it is strong and simple and its natural symmetry balances flying forces better."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:81
#: ccefe8708dd049feb351915cfa16d628
msgid "A humming bird sized `Estes Proto X <http://www.estesrockets.com/helis-quads/quadcopters/004606-proto-x>`__ is shown below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:88
#: 4055160e3d68418e80e0f4f362dd7551
msgid "A fifteen thousand dollar SteadyDrone Q4D-X Quadcopter with 28\" propellers, 8KG lifting capability and claimed 60 minute flight times."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:95
#: 618ff03fb3264b7cb7ce39335820bd7d
msgid "For professional use, HexaCopters and OctoCopters with 6 and 8 Motor/propeller propulsion units are popular."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:98
#: be8affc53c58424fb496dd3f1d214628
msgid "Hexacopters, Octocopters, Hex Y's and Octo X's can provide stable heavy lift platforms good for photography and other uses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:100
#: fd04195b628b4004a925a1b210b277f4
msgid "Hex and Octocopters may have the benefit of potentially being able to continue to fly with a single motor failure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:102
#: b901a33fb37146b383e6135e5c8f5754
msgid "However the increased complexity versus a Quadcopter makes them more failure prone."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:104
#: d2638d199f9f46d4a7bfcb606fb9f953
msgid "The reduction in prop size and increase in prop speed result in a smoother flight than an equivalent large blade Quadcopter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:106
#: fa91a61f4fef4b8885e0ab590d3c3178
msgid "However it also results in some reduction in flight efficiency and endurance all other things being equal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:112
#: a8fa5f614e7f4ced8b9d0a54bc148eae
msgid "Hex Y6 and Octo X8 designs with pairs of coaxial motor/propeller units mounted back to back are also becoming popular."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:114
#: 526c58d5ff84457e9dda20342cd2e73f
msgid "Singlecopters and Coax copters are very new designs and have some advantages in specific applications."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:117
#: 65767247813545c1a0fbde692d63011e
msgid "Since they tend to a single ducted body for either the one or two motor/propeller units they tend to be self protected indoors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:119
#: c187c046565445fb8fc90e37666d72ce
msgid "The coax copter which relies on variable thrust on each of its 2 props for rotation is functionally simpler than the single copter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:121
#: c70ea8bb59c94839bb54719ffdf661e2
msgid "The side profile of the ducted body makes these copters more susceptible to winds outdoors requiring more effort to compensate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:123
#: 1be6733f560646d5968f1f58699b5608
msgid "While generally good at hovering and fine positioning, they are more speed and performance limited than other multicopter designs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:125
#: 6421b6842059477e9fab134f32eae313
msgid "The Singlecopter in particular is reasonably adaptable to gasoline engines for much greater endurance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:127
#: 9b5f1950a46a4249813fd4bc015099d3
msgid "The possibility of using a single large propeller implies that good efficiencies could be realized even with an electric versions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:130
#: e381245f57ef4f92b773253a72b3932e
msgid "The Singlecopter features a single motor/propeller unit with 4 servo controlled vanes to direct roll, pitch and yaw."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:136
#: 73e490fa6ecc4a41bf0b84e9b3072999
msgid "The Coaxcopter has dual motor/propeller units for thrust and yaw control and 2 servo controlled vanes for roll and  pitch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:142
#: fcaa4da6e11844af841d3eaf90d1496f
msgid "There are also variable pitch Multicopters for incredible acrobatic performance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:145
#: b96d4276869a458882d634be2078a5e0
msgid "Variable pitch multicopters have some interesting potential uses as well like the `Curtis Youngblood Stingray 500 <http://curtisyoungblood.com/V2/products/quadcopters/stingray-500>`__ shown below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:147
#: c850ad296b2e4b349bc766a84694a869
msgid "Servo control of the props (rotors) produces roll, pitch and yaw so they are often powered by a single motor with shaft or belt drive."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:150
#: 3f63d3ce1c724f509443cde219b89a43
msgid "If you use a single motor it is feasible to use a gasoline engine giving you the potential for considerable endurance and range."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:152
#: 58cf2da27c244216862d75b358df39f4
msgid "These are very high performance and can even fly inverted, they are also mechanically more complex but can be built robustly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:158
#: 6d36fc2c628745c2a36e2c6d0fb5f20f
msgid "And copters with more than 8 motor/propeller units may be useful for specialized, extreme `(or insane) <https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=L75ESD9PBOw>`__ applications."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:166
#: 9a5d309b38db440e9a0786a0b8b85007
msgid "Motors, propellers and ESCs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:168
#: 4745894631ce447283853461ce92333b
msgid "For multicopters, motors, propellers and ESCs (speed controllers) are critical and have been failure prone in the past."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:171
#: e31c057d3cdc464f8c85058a7ed9d767
msgid "This ECalc based `Xcopter: motor - propeller - battery - ESC calculator <https://www.ecalc.ch/xcoptercalc.php?ecalc&lang=en>`__ will help you pick the best components for your copter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:174
#: 94fb4ebe729e48eead42150270ce093b
msgid "Quadcopter design will be used for illustration as they are the most wide spread and the most versatile."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:177
#: c2e640aa089c4bc48a18e28c4342aeec
msgid "But the information applies equally to Hex and Octo designs, either conventional or coaxial Y and X types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:180
#: 47200ee613584ac0bfdeba9ae2a5099b
msgid "The brushless out-runner motors have to support the full weight of the copter continuously while turning at high speed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:183
#: b0e3187728d34143a51de5a0f3ccf838
msgid "Hobby grade motors have often used inadequate Conrad type unsealed bearings which are good axially but not in thrust."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:186
#: 827a0d8b85f3424daafd8dbbe55d7752
msgid "And the motors are usually open frame to permit the greatest cooling but providing little or no protection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:188
#: d1047787753143fa92b9bd8b605f1d73
msgid "This has meant an unnecessarily high failure rate and very poor survival in wet or dusty conditions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:190
#: 2b08edf332bc4fd99a8dc20a742a2849
msgid "The cheapest possible Chinese motor is never a good choice for something that literally hangs in the air by its motor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:193
#: 18fc38f17bfa44a6aa2fb2703df1b368
msgid "Some of the best motors have 2 or better 3 easily replaceable ABEC-7 bearings, RCTiger-Motor Pro series and KDE for instance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:196
#: fb69e2d9afec4237a4645d3013e7df7f
msgid "The best motors are well ventilated, made with high temperature components and coated and sealed for environmental protection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:198
#: fc88b19bd02e4b0cb20df9e3a445719e
msgid "The best motors like TMotor and KDE have performance comparison charts, these should be reviewed when designing a copter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:200
#: aacfed6526eb46faa325cc4b4e21b0f9
msgid "You are best off selecting motor - prop - battery cell combinations that will provide 10% or higher G/W efficiency at 50% throttle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:203
#: e6e9151a524740269fb6ca9a43ff919f
msgid "You should also target you copter design weight so that it hovers at approximately 50% throttle for optimum efficiency and flight time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:206
#: 28cdf275e59c4b078c15cb6d8f30ceca
msgid "Top motors can cost considerably more, but reliability, performance and efficiency can be much better and worth it in the long run."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:209
#: 91000b8891664820bd33ffaf66af39f0
msgid "Low KV motors running on lower voltage (fewer cells) with large propellers are the most efficient and provide the longest flight times."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:213
#: 753cee387ea744b585ed73d873c46cd6
msgid "Selecting the best motor, propeller, battery set will enable you to build a copter with a usable 30 minute flight time including a camera."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:217
#: 506302e54dbe42e292f1dc71b9066a0d
msgid "You can get 30 minutes from 330 copters with 8\" props to 700 size copters with 18\" props depending on camera / gimbal weight."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:220
#: 4b84798261234bf0ba4d7c92e9cc02d4
msgid "It is very hard to get much more than 30 minutes of usable flight time from any \"useful\" multicopter regardless of size."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:222
#: cfab4a66affc4a6d9b7e6fa81dfabc69
msgid "For hobby grade components, 20 minute maximum flight times would be a more realistic goal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:225
#: 9d9b07e4d48049b58df5e96d42f25323
msgid "ESCs are also very important."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:227
#: 6a6ea2c161f944c8bfba660941f22e21
msgid "High quality ESCs are more reliable than cheap ones."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:228
#: d0380103855c46ad8f17b24882504f92
msgid "And ESCs need to be properly sized to ensure they can provide the maximum current that is necessary."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:231
#: 593b572fe66442b0a3e1462fd3e7a9a0
msgid "Generally use the right size not over sized because they are more efficient if operated in the appropriate range (and lighter)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:235
#: 201db123eb5b4ccda5474aaf70ec4321
msgid "Sufficient cooling is also very important especially for \"Heavy Lift\" copters, and the ESCs may need to be placed in the air stream."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:238
#: 93cc8a628fed4cd0894b5c0b85b2c4c1
msgid "For small to medium QuadCopters there are four in one ESCs in the 20 - 30 Amp size range with several advantages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:241
#: 8a1906e7d023488b9fdd775a7f203754
msgid "They eliminate the need for a power distribution plate or block and all the attendant wiring."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:243
#: c75715f831b341869e75744d9be50b74
msgid "The considerable reduction in DC wiring results in less DC EMF radiation interference with the compass."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:245
#: 8d65a8f543674ea587939b296a88c42d
msgid "They can often be conveniently installed tidily in the center of the copter frame."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:247
#: cef4c17af11f40ffb83ed6362e76ec6d
msgid "The 20 and 25 amp ones work with 3 or 4 cell LiPo batteries and the 30 amp one works with 3 to 6 cell batteries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:249
#: 7beb5f4b480d4f3d94660d787b4254c6
msgid "They have a built in aluminum heat sink plate on one side (which you can augment with a finned heat sink if necessary)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:251
#: 240e49682e7047c992a03f1ef092e4a4
msgid "You can use a thin layer of Fujik silicone thermal glue to attach a finned heat sink if one is needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:253
#: 185ddd67953b44ad8dbd4407e0afffcd
msgid "They generally have higher reliability than individual ESCs and are reasonably priced."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:256
#: 649f5150594b4c1bad29382c49c0f679
msgid "Larger diameter slower turning propellers are normally a lot more efficient than smaller, faster ones."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:259
#: f112971c8f5c423fba4dadfeef945a0e
msgid "But there are limits and drawbacks:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:261
#: c19d98a6fd5246798321d58556c4689c
msgid "Trying to turn too large a prop for a given motor can cause it to overheat so motors usually have a maximum prop size."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:263
#: 4831d97756604f18b5e7a088b19227a4
msgid "Also, really large, slow props can reduce the responsiveness of the multicopter and even cause it to oscillate in the air or vibrate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:266
#: bc260d328dac49c0a20171c42c252b22
msgid "Unless taken to extremes these difficulties are not usually significant and can be compensated for by various means."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:268
#: 9ed1d44d2f644819b2a234451894eab3
msgid "And you can always drop the diameter an inch if the handling characteristics or motor stress are not what you want."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:271
#: 4aae84782c5442b081889840440b54b6
msgid "There are also different designs of propellers and for larger ones turning at slower speeds design is especially critical."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:274
#: 7a70714912b244efab68ebac14b4eb3a
msgid "Carbon fiber designs with cupped blades that are wider at the hub and narrower at the tip are best for larger sizes 14\" and over."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:277
#: 235fbd776d1c4b9a925359d174082da3
msgid "Smaller ones in the 14\" and under category can be of more conventional design with a wider than normal blade and of plastic or CF."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:280
#: 919e94fd9e9e402787a31b6b463df0f8
msgid "Often motors are \"charted\" with specific propellers and these are certainly the best starting point for optimum performance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:282
#: e94f56a34a614c018b373df0ce32d0ec
msgid "TMotor is considered a premium prop, but good results have been obtained with RC-Timer and Tarot in the large tapered props."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:284
#: 201f352a59b046b0a36c43e593cf1693
msgid "APC, DJI, GemFan, RC Drones and Graupner all produce good props in the 14\" and under category."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:288
#: a1985e4793a4487ab5704282c0548b81
msgid "Professional Grade Power System for large Quadcopters (28\" Propellers)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:290
#: de562193d4a84f48b3b2aff9536506e8
msgid "The `Tigermotor U8 Pro Series <http://www.rctigermotor.com/html/2013/Efficiency-Type_1219/176.html>`__ motor is currently top of the line for a commercially available (large) copter motor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:294
#: 58fa2d05ce8e42189dd7df20d77faf91
msgid "It features Environmentally protected, closed construction and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:295
#: b251e01bfa404020a22a3917721660b9
msgid "easily replaceable bearings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:300
#: d8826de249304034b91371a7a2b19602
msgid "They have very high quality two piece 27, 28 and 29\" carbon fiber propellers for them as well"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:306
#: 620935e013b74ec7a72265775d56bd22
msgid "And a top quality 70 AMP ESC (speed controller) to go with it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:311
#: 39125c45032e450a93d8468f8b29ff29
msgid "U8 Pro T-Motor $300.00, 28\" CF Props $370.00 a pair, 70 Amp Pro ESC $110.00 @ four each = $2380.00."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:313
#: 276d58797e48492e80cc1dacec5d238b
msgid "These are used in the large Steadidrone Quadcopter shown above, clearly a top quality professional and expensive product."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:315
#: 10df7793a93a4542b8fb6b40abd4f000
msgid "This is a very heavy lift and long endurance copter and is completely excessive and hazardous for most uses and needs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:317
#: be61808a601b4e52a63211f3a4b8618f
