#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:496
#: 01fcf19d14794333a675ea5ca76b90a0
msgid "The MultiCopter Frame"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:498
#: fd7aaac88d6e4b0e9363ff97141517a4
msgid "There are many types of frames and it is most important to put together a frame that is appropriate for your use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:500
#: 576985532b6249a3b49c024c49f6ad36
msgid "There are a lot of Multicopter frame types and many are available as bare frame kits or Almost Ready To Fly or Ready To Fly copters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:502
#: ffd703393342440faf5434b8d0bcab24
msgid "Most professional grade Multicopters are made from fiberglass and carbon fiber cut tubing and plate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:504
#: ea926e763a4c44429148db6e3046d0af
msgid "Carbon fiber is very strong, but is also brittle and can shatter on impact, it is also hard to machine and to glue to."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:506
#: 1a0c21604d5149c98a97fb30c7914b34
msgid "Fiberglass weighs a bit more for equivalent strength but is more shatter resistant and easier to machine and glue to."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:508
#: 8f45cffeb37846bba8193f586d1e1e86
msgid "Fiberglass or carbon fiber tube and sheet construction are very suitable to use for making your own copters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:511
#: 6cdb1345a35849959dd5e2fa78bdd109
msgid "Many consumer grade Multicopters are made with injection molded plastic parts and aluminum tubing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:514
#: 5187887188574194837e51eca35fa749
msgid "Some injection molded parts can be very durable (the Iris's Zytel frame arms for instance), but others are cheap and break easily."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:517
#: 1d88de0927764779be4d3d45910aeb16
msgid "Square aluminum tubing frame arms are common, but they tend to bend or break with annoying frequency in normal mishaps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:519
#: 6533452f3388477098d20e5cd4f077e9
msgid "Except in specialized welded H or box frames aluminum tubing frame arms are sub optimal and will not be covered in depth here."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:523
#: 80c5a0176b534b43afda20e0ae82cfc2
msgid "Some of the newer, smaller, commercially made Quadcopters have monolithic injection molded plastic shells."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:526
#: 9115f6dc424541ddaa5391bb43ba47b0
msgid "On smaller copters these shells can be quite durable but they would be too fragile on larger ones even if mold costs were justified."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:530
#: d700750b634746d9afdaefc9c6d011ca
msgid "A few Quadcopters have monolithic shells made from vacuum formed laminated Kydex or other plastic sheet"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:533
#: ef498f1cc1594aca8ce4215b46472cc0
msgid "Vacuum formed shells of laminated Kydex have proven very durable on small copters and are very good for waterproof uses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:535
#: a210b7d4ffa74e08928c4a92f1acd412
msgid "At least one vacuum formed copter has been made with built in blade guards the Safe Flight 4410 (unfortunately out of business)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:539
#: a4acac5831f240199c143e8e66bf641e
msgid "Hand laid fiberglass or carbon fiber is also popular on high end quadcopters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:542
#: 284559e26d874310a641b32451081ecf
msgid "There are some very attractive, hard to get and not inexpensive hand laid fiberglass and carbon fiber shells made by \"DeX\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:544
#: f9f26c33dcaa4d0791231c3d21d384c2
msgid "There are also a variety of fiberglass shells for civilian, commercial and military use including an amphibious one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:546
#: 484bb5027478496db527d67844a996ed
msgid "Fiberglass shells tend to be expensive and may get damaged in use and can be difficult to repair."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:549
#: 56d10dd9af7f4266bf95b64f77d5551f
msgid "Each type of construction has advantages and disadvantages and it is very important to figure out what is important for your needs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:551
#: 609d5f93fc4140b5868533090a3cb1eb
msgid "Prop to prop and prop to frame clearance limit the max diameter of your propeller blades."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:554
#: ef1577e0af4f49429625730d363c24e6
msgid "Allowing for various prop diameters will let you tune the copter for its current weight, batteries and function.."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:556
#: 8a819c1d35224429a62b4ab0ce893b56
msgid "Generally allow an additional half inch of clearance from prop tip to tip or to center frame to avoid asymmetrical prop wash vibration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:559
#: 138f4349a328429fbf877618fe1e853c
msgid "A major design criteria is to size the frame appropriately for the largest propellers you might ever want to use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:561
#: f3a66982a11042348c0c12cc7af467ed
msgid "Generally bigger propeller diameter equals better efficiency and an X frame layout normally permits the largest possible props."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:564
#: b01e79ed27bb4276afcde094d03f6b9e
msgid "Of course the motor speed and power and frame strength have to be matched to the propeller diameter and to total lifting capacity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:567
#: 5449b97cb403448bb648d933073dba18
msgid "Pancake Low KV, Low RPM motors can turn bigger propellers efficiently."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:569
#: ce0a217e8bb44c99a208261cbeae42d5
msgid "It is possible to overlap prop tips if you have one above the other, but it does affect efficiency and induces asymmetric vibration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:572
#: 3ed337d221234b52ac7c08a06c6b3e7b
msgid "Big slow props can have adverse vibration, instability, gust compensation and response rate issues also so that is a downside."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:576
#: e65c97c05f4749b787a4b49b651ce527
msgid "The additional motors of Hex and Octocopters can permit single motor out recovery and provide for smoother flight for photo uses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:579
#: 08dbf82875e24b15901fba710d2f5c52
msgid "But they need to use smaller propellers because of motor to motor clearance which is less efficient resulting in shorter flight times."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:582
#: ccb8263c6afd4855b8d920052812281d
msgid "There is also additional cost and weight of the frames and extra motors and propellers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:584
#: a941850ff1b14673b267ae67bbcf2bd8
msgid "And, the overall increase in complexity also reduces reliability."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:586
#: 0756faee0d1f416db88f4aea2575a674
msgid "High quality extended service larger pancake motors and props are just starting to become available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:588
#: 1b6e3e5c21b6459d8459a84f753762ae
msgid "So we are likely to see a shift to large Quadcopters from Hexacopters and Octocopters even for professional and commercial uses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:593
#: 6838dabd60904e82b750442c2bc7989e
msgid "The Carbon Fiber or Fiberglass Tube and Plate Frame"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:595
#: 02d1c1543e2345adb6812e954c12e65d
msgid "The carbon fiber or fiberglass tube and plate frame is popular because it is strong and light and easily manufactured."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:598
#: 83ac972096fb46358476576103343a72
msgid "The `Tarot 650 <http://www.helipal.com/tarot-fy650-quadricopter-frame-set.html>`__ is a typical layout medium sized carbon fiber Quadcopter frame that can work with up to 17\" propellers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:602
#: 8c4c52d427a14982aa58ab37eba0c2cd
msgid "It features folding arms and landing gear."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:603
#: f5875bc6fff34565be363d04a5a74401
msgid "Its ability to support pancake motors and 17\" props means it can provide long flight times."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:605
#: ba20dffb6c5a41fd93fd2d275ea15adf
msgid "Some people have said the quality of construction is not as good as it could be but for $125.00 it is an amazing bargain."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:611
#: 0db51812d29a4d3b95b4691763c1556d
msgid "Fabrication requirements and techniques for fiberglass and carbon fiber tube and plate copters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:613
#: 4cfbeba2e6134bbcbf385e4bfd5f958b
msgid "On the copters shown above the method of attachment is by clamping carbon fiber tube frame arms with aluminum brackets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:616
#: 4ff42f2ca715466e9ef3ec1a77ac8fd7
msgid "This is because of the difficulties in attaching carbon fiber parts as well as the stress that can result from drilling the tubing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:619
#: e1b7746f3e6a45209c713ff9426e8178
msgid "Fiberglass is not quite as strong or light as carbon fiber but it is more flexible and easier to join and machine."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:622
#: 505a44eb164149ce8ccd253add3a89b8
msgid "If what you need is available in a commercial frame kit you are normally better off buying it as you will spend more making your own."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:625
#: 8e4d517d3cf64d939f41925a21c47e1c
msgid "It will also take a lot of time and effort to design the copter, to obtain the components and to, cut, drill, machine and fabricate them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:628
#: 018240e7eba34ebb8228e01c4acb05c2
msgid "There is also a strong possibility that design and fabrication mistakes and misperceptions will require that some things get redone."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:632
#: 264641ebf05249d4b87afb9636f9a6e8
msgid "If you have sufficient reason to make your own frame, tube and plate construction is generally the most practical for home production."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:634
#: 636caf7d576b46afa5e278b410fd7afd
msgid "It is reasonable to mix materials, commonly carbon fiber frame tubes and fiberglass central and motor mounting plates."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:637
#: 158e6cc9cb9d406eb37dee082908269b
msgid "Carbon fiber and fiberglass tubing and plate can be cut with a hacksaw or power jig or band saw (with metal or fiberglass blades)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:641
#: 8b6487d827df4be8802e05e64ba66a80
msgid "It can also be drilled and milled with HSS or TC coated drills and mills, but all tooling wears out very quickly cutting these materials."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:645
#: 14d9f77f352f4d9f8b4c62d92a69b301
msgid "Carbon fiber in particular is tricky to cut, drill and machine, it can tear, shatter or de-laminate if not done smoothly and slowly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:648
#: 2084f6f6c47d45f59731081dff4efb81
msgid "A drill press is mandatory for carbon fiber, you can't center punch a pilot drill hole, so it needs to be held precisely in place."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:651
#: fd927d71275d470f9f9a6edee8de4ef4
msgid "Avoid milling of carbon fiber if at all possible, it is very difficult to accomplish satisfactory results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:653
#: eac7d8879ef6456cb1ef1b1a6df12a2a
msgid "You will see carbon fiber plates that have milled slots on consumer copters but these have generally been cut with a water jet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:656
#: dec871b41450435d8a34eb7eb447f3fc
msgid "With carbon fiber you will generally get better results drilling precision placed holes rather than attempting to mill slots in it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:659
#: bc79acb4c039458aacb4a61357785fd6
msgid "You can carefully and slowly cut a carbon fiber plates exterior edges with a power saw and smooth them with a Dremel tool."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:661
#: 5fa43d76f96043ee8124bc6fc1d2cb91
msgid "If you must put in slots consider drilling a hole at each end and using a small circular saw on a Dremel or flex shaft to connect them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:665
#: 45bdc80c6d5c442fa10f31c53869366e
msgid "It will be necessary to provide appropriate brackets to clamp the motor mounts and central hub to the frame arm tubes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:668
#: bd634790ee9d4dc6a51f3b4e5c7de9c4
msgid "Tubing needs to be clamped but must not be \"crushed\", silicone or rubber gasket can provide protection and vibration isolation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:670
#: e1d9c748e7bf45f3be9d71a39710ebb9
msgid "Hardware should be aluminum or stainless steel machine screws and you can use Nylok nuts or \"Blue\" Loctite on regular nuts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/advanced-multicopter-design.rst:672
#: 1ffc4e7bc3814aa991a2c6ab51db97a0
msgid "Plate separation and mounting can be provided with Nylon or aluminum standoffs."
msgstr ""

